    {
      "charging_model": "Jobs consume Service Units (SU). 1 SU corresponds to one compute core using less than approximately 2 GB of memory for one hour. Partitions have charging factors (e.g., highmem nodes charged 4 SU per compute core). Node-exclusive partitions allocate an entire node and jobs are charged for the full-node allocation (example: charged for 128 cores).",
      "note": "Combined statements: SU definition, highmem multiplier, node-exclusive behavior and example.",
